8. node.get(i) may return null if index out of bounds? But loop bound ensures i < node.size() and tupleSchema size, so safe. However if node is an array but contains null elements (i.e., JSON null), node.get(i) returns NullNode, not null reference. That's okay.

9. atPath(at,i) may throw NullPointerException if at is null? Let's check atPath method in BaseJsonValidator (not shown). Likely it concatenates path; may NPE if at null. So test at null.

10. atPath may produce invalid path but not exception.

